<iframe src="../../media/desmos/73a41d9f6d133fb73de34f9f4ccacd50756a4c9c.html" width="500" height="400"/><para>What is the equation for the curve of best fit that models the data?</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise id="_2bb7ca48-10c1-470e-8d66-afc1bebad136" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(y = -0.93x^2+ 22.63x + 10.48\)</para><para>\(y = -0.69x^2+ 24.83x + 8.07\)</para><para>\(y = -3.11x^2+ 16.32x + 8.94\)</para><para>\(y = -0.7x^2 + 35.93x + 8.19\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.12.2.</para><para>The correct answer is \(y = -0.69x^2+ 24.83x + 8.07\).
     </para></solution></exercise></section><!--2-->
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
