<section class="check-understanding"><exercise id="_57966c39-30be-48a6-8aeb-6e20d037a229" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(y = -25.41x^2+ 59.28x + 9.64\)</para><para>\(y = -30.84x^2+ 49.61x + 8.99\)</para><para>\(y = -3.72x^2 + 7.34x + 8.67\)</para><para>\(y = -35.78x^2+ 45.21x + 3.74\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 8.12.2.</para><para>The correct answer is \(y = -25.41x^2+ 59.28x + 9.64\).
     </para></solution></exercise></section><!--5-->
<para>For questions 5 – 9, use the following information.</para>
<para><quote>The path of a toy rocket after launch is modeled by the following data set. The height of the rocket, in feet, \(y\), corresponds to the number of seconds passed, \(x\).</quote></para><iframe src="../../media/desmos/9c35f4a1131f245ab788215077a301fd3447ea4a.html" width="500" height="400"/><section class="check-understanding"><exercise id="b90b03f7-6d4e-43e9-ab11-78fd7d4711c5" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What is the equation for the curve of best fit that models the flight of the toy rocket?</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(y = -6.1x^2+ 31x + 1.24\)</para><para>\(y = -11.9x^2+ 30.2x + 3.64\)</para><para>\(y = -4.2x^2 + 34x + 6.34\)</para><para>\(y = -9.2x^2+ 46x + 3.51\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.12.3.</para><para>The correct answer is \(y = -9.2x^2+ 46x + 3.51\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_147dbf86-c93a-48c1-ab7f-05529b149e93" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Approximately how high will the rocket be 2 seconds after launch?</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>45.91 feet</para><para>53.60 feet</para><para>58.71 feet</para><para>61.00 feet</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 8.12.3.</para><para>The correct answer is 58.71 feet.
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_436af224-3161-411e-8ab5-eb1def5c2205" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>At what approximate times after launch will the rocket have a height of 20 feet?</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>0.26 seconds after launch and 4.74 seconds after launch</para><para>0.39 seconds after launch and 4.61 seconds after launch</para><para>0.52 seconds after launch and 4.48 seconds after launch</para><para>0.82 seconds after launch and 4.18 seconds after launch</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.12.3.</para><para>The correct answer is 0.39 seconds after launch and 4.61 seconds after launch.</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_16d27a20-3e37-4123-b6d5-1fadbc84bd28" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Approximately how long will it take the rocket to reach its maximum height?</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>1.73 seconds</para><para>2.50 seconds</para><para>3.20 seconds</para><para>5.08 seconds</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.12.3.</para><para>The correct answer is 2.50 seconds.
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_15839ded-e850-4b5f-8918-5debe5f219e3" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Approximately how long will it take for the rocket to land on the ground?</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>2.50 seconds</para><para>4.63 seconds</para><para>5.08 seconds</para><para>6.12 seconds</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.12.3.</para><para>The correct answer is 5.08 seconds.</para></solution></exercise></section><!--10 prelude -->
<para>For question 10, Maria has found a curve of best fit using the equation below.</para>
<iframe src="../../media/desmos/dc8c59067ba553f99987d0ad5b784b8d94eb5657.html" width="500" height="400"/><section class="check-understanding"><exercise id="_50848151-29ad-4f88-a8a1-521249bd70f8" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What is the \(y\)-value Maria is asked to predict?</para><para>Maria is asked to predict the \(y\)-value on her curve when \(x = 10\). To do this, she graphs the function \(x = 10\) and analyzes the intersection point of the curve and the line.</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>10</para><para>93</para><para>105</para><para>111</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.12.4.</para><para>The correct answer is 111.</para></solution></exercise></section></section>
